MODULE largerecords;
  (* Phase 11 D4: a record's LLVM type used to be spelled out inline, and
     one whose spelling passed 799 characters (160 INTEGER fields, fewer
     wide ones) halted poc with an index-range error. Records are named
     struct types now (LLVMTypes, "Named struct types"). Wide has 400
     fields; it is nested in records, in arrays of records, in an inline
     anonymous record and a procedure-local record, and every one is
     assigned whole, passed by value and through a pointer. voc prints the
     same under both size models. *)
